<H1>Medium data</H1>
Search for medium no. = [923].
<HR>
Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121&#176;C for 15 min.
<HR>
<P><B><FONT SIZE=3>923&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;PEAT MEDIUM 1 FOR METHANOREGURA BOONEI</FONT></B></P>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Major metals (see below)                               </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;10.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Trace metal 1 solution (see below)                      </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water                                         </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> L  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Mix components thoroughly and adjust pH to 5.0 with HCl.  Bring to a boil for 5 min, then, cool down under a stream of a N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20, v/v) gas mixture.  Distribute the medium into Balch-type culture tubes (5 ml each) under the same gas mixture, seal with thick blue butyl rubber stoppers and autoclave.  <br>
To complete the medium, replace the gas phase with H<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20, v/v) gas mixture, and add the following solutions to each of the culture tubes (containing 5 ml medium) from sterile anaerobic stocks (autoclaved or *filter-sterilized):  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 83 mM TiNTA solution* (see below)                       </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.06&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 0.5 M HOMOPIPES solution* (pH 5.4)                      </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.05&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Vitamin solution* (see below)                           </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.05&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 2% Yeast extract solution                              </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.05&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 50 mM Coenzyme M solution                               </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.05&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 20 mM Sodium acetate                                    </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.05&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Check the final pH of the medium to be about 5.1.  Pressurize inoculated tubes to 70 kPa H<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20, v/v).  <br>
<I>Major metals:</I> <br>
